## **4. Technical Constraints & Non-Functional Realities**

* **Rate Limiting Handling:** According to the official Slack documentation, `chat.postMessage` is classified as a **Tier 3 Rate Limit** tier (allowing an average operational threshold of **1 write per second per channel**). If an email thread bursts with multiple attachments or updates simultaneously, our internal NATS JetStream queue must execute message batching or exponential backoff using HTTP 429 Retry-After response headers.
* **Message Formatting Alignment:** Text coming from Email contains rich text or raw HTML (`<div>`, `<p>`). Text inside Slack relies strictly on specialized mrkdwn parsing constraints (e.g., `<http://url|text>`). Our gateway transformer must map and parse HTML string inputs into structural Slack block element schemas prior to execution payload transmission.